;; db: bench_walk
;; The hub pathology inside RECURSION: each newly visited node expands
;; through the hub to every spoke (redge then sedge = n candidates), and
;; the attributed tree edge (tedge C A W: C is a child of A) keeps only
;; its real children.  The semijoin filter probes tedge on A right after
;; the driver, so a leaf's visit costs one probe instead of an n-way
;; expansion -- and 15/16 of the tree is leaves.  Exercises filters on
;; every iteration of a fixpoint (tree depth ~4).
table (redge int int)
table (sedge int int)
table (tedge int int int)
table (visit int)

rule (visit A) (redge A B) (sedge B C) (tedge C A W) --> (visit C)
